WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.467
-Mike Myers, welcome back.
We love having you on the show.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.667
-Thank you.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:05.834
-Thanks for being here.
-Lovely to be here.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.767
-We have a lot of things
we have to get into

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.167
and talk about.
-Sure.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.067
-But backstage, you just told me
something very interesting.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:14.467
I know you were a big fan
of the queen.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.100
-I was, in fact, yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.501
-I am Canadian, you see.
-Yes.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.901
Can you tell everyone
what you told me --

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.167
you went to Buckingham Palace?

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.501
-I went to Buckingham Palace
with Steve Higgins.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.133
That's right.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:28.167
Not recently,
but a couple of years ago,

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:33.067
and a friend of mine arranged
for Steve and I to

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.634
watch the changing of the guard

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.601
from inside
Buckingham Palace's gates.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:39.968
-Wow.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:43.634
-We went through a rigorous
security, background check

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.033
and all this stuff.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.968
Being of English -- My parents
are from Liverpool, England,

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.000
so it's like,
a huge, huge deal.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
-Of course.
-And we got let in.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.300
And then the band come out,
and they're playing

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.367
that, you know --
♪ Ba-da-da-da-da ♪

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.400
You know, all that --

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.334
[ Imitates fanfare ]

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.834
And I'm like,
"Oh, this is so amazing."

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.467
And then they break into
the "Austin Powers" theme.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:05.634
[ Laughing ]

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.767
-And they started playing
"Soul Bossa Nova."

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.133
And it's like --
[ Sings "Soul Bossa Nova" ]

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.667
[ Band plays "Soul Bossa Nova" ]
There you go!

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.834
[ Singing along ] You know?

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.133
-I mean --
-And I just --

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.267
I couldn't believe it.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.000
One of the guards walked by
holding a flag,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.434
and they're not
supposed to talk.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:26.200
He goes, "Oh, I bet you've heard
this song before, Mr. Myers."

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.400
And I'm like,
"Don't talk to me!"

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.968
-"You're not allowed to talk!"
-"Don't talk!"

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.100
"I'm Canadian,
I'm gonna get in trouble!"

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.234
-How cool is that?
That's amazing.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:33.834
-Yeah.
-Speaking of Austin Powers,

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:37.901
though, we've talked about it on
the show a bunch of times.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.667
Would you ever do another
Austin Powers?

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.167
Would you ever do
anther "Wayne's World"?

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.033
These are rumors that
I'm starting.

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:47.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.100
We don't have an applause sign!

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.234
They're doing that
because they love this!

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.300
-Aww.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.400
-Would you do another
Austin Powers?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.634
Do you have something
to announce?

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.133
-No, I don't have anything
to announce.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:00.367
I -- I can neither confirm
nor deny the existence

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.000
or non-existence of
such a project.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.400
-Yeah.
-Um, yeah.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.000
I would love to do it.
Of course. It's fun.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.033
-Yeah.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.400
-What do you need?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.400
How do we make this happen?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.968
What would it be --
How can I --

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.434
What can we do?

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.868
A Dr. Evil spin-off?

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:18.334
-I just, you know, I have three
kids under the age of 11.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.901
I've been super, super busy
being a dad.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.100
-I know, but come on!

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.634
We want more! We want more
from you, Mike Myers!

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.200
-Alright.
-We need ya!

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.167
-I'll see what I can do,
Jimmy Fallon.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.501
-Thank you very much.
-Very good.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.334
-I want to hear about
"Amsterdam."

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.667
-Sure.

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.234
-We had Robert de Niro
on the show, but what a cast.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.567
Margot Robbie, Christian Bale.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:41.601
-No, it was like doing a movie
at Madame Tussaud's.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.234
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:46.667
-I was so intimidated.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.901
-Chris Rock and I were just
watching the rest of the cast,

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.000
and we were like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.434
Actors are awesome,
aren't they?"

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.834
-No, please.
-They're just --

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.267
It was just
absolutely intimidating.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.901
-How's David O'Russell?
-David O'Russell's a genius.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.834
-He's one of the best directors.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.133
He's an American auteur.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:05.634
It was one of the most creative,
fantastic experiences.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.234
I was super sad when
it was over.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:10.801
And it was just,
everybody pulled together.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.667
It was an unbelievable --

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.133
-Did you talk much with
De Niro?

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.701
-I did, but I was too
intimidated, you know?

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:18.300
Because it's sort of like
being in a scene

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.133
with the Eiffel Tower, you know?

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.467
It's like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.434
Those are the molecules that
make up Robert de Niro."

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.300
-Yeah, he's the real deal.
-Holy crap.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.467
And he was super lovely.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.534
He's very introverted
and very, very nice,

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:31.367
and I just -- I didn't want to
take up any of his time.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.901
So he'd be like,
"Do you live in New York?"

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.400
And I'd be like, "Yeah,
I live in New York.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.501
I love it. Great."

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:37.834
We'd just sort of like --

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:40.200
Don't talk to him. Don't take up
any more of his time.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.801
"Aren't you from Toronto?"
"I'm from Toronto.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.567
I live in New York.
I love New York." Done.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:46.400
-He's like,
"Mike Myers is weird."

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.234
-"This guys' bizarre."

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:51.434
And I developed this laugh, too,
so he'd be like,

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:53.701
"On night shoots,
do you drink coffee?"

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.167
I'd go -- [Laughing],
"Yeah, I do."

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.901
I don't have that laugh!

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.267
I've never had that laugh.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.200
You kept doing it?
-Oh, my God.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.701
[Laughing] "Yeah, you know.
It's great."

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.100
-"You like coffee?" [Giggling]

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.868
[Laughing throughout] "Yeah,
I love coffee, who doesn't?"

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:09.367
-[Laughing] "Milk, sometimes,
cream in the coffee, sugar."

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.467
-"Yeah, sometimes sugar."
[Laughing]

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.701
-You're like, "What am I doing?"
-What an idiot.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:16.167
-Do you stay in character
when you're in that character?

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:17.467
-I've always done.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.901
I've always stayed in character,

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.133
and now it's just superstition,
at this point.

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.634
And I thought, "is this weird?"

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:26.701
And then Christian Bale
also stays in character all day.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.367
And because of
the improvisational nature

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:32.000
of the movie, I was never sure
when the day was done

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.834
and I could talk in
my normal accent again.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:37.334
Neither did Christian Bale,
so I ran into him

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.934
in front of his trailer,
and he's English, right?

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.868
He's from Wales, but he has
an English accent,

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.501
but he's playing an American.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:46.667
And I'm North American,
playing an English person,

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.067
and so he's sort of like,

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.834
[In character accent]
"Where ya from, mate?"

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:52.267
[In character accent] "Well,
actually, I'm from Toronto."

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.501
And I thought, "Am I...?"

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.167
-What a brain workout!

00:04:57.167 --> 00:05:01.868
-I'm like, "I'm not gonna break.
I'm not gonna break.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.033
I'm committed."

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.467
-That's really fun.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:07.133
-[As Christian Bale] "No, I'm
from a small town in Wales."

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.567
And I'm like, "Well, see, I'm
from the suburbs of Toronto.

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.901
Terribly English.

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:16.701
-Hockey.
-I love hockey and maple syrup,

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:19.801
mountains and all that."

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:22.434
-Can we tell everyone
what "Amsterdam" is about?

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.067
It's a comedic thriller.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.534
-It is.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:30.067
"Amsterdam" is about
three friends --

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.601
It takes place in the '30s.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:35.501
It's a beautiful,
beautifully made movie.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.133
I'm so thrilled to
be part of it.

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:38.634
It's about friendship,

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.868
and it basically asks
the question about,

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.000
"What is your Amsterdam?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.267
What is your favorite time
in your life?"

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:47.300
And we see their favorite time

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.634
set against an unbelievably
and historically accurate,

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.100
fascinating intrigue.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.167
-I like
"What is your Amsterdam?"

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:55.334
That's pretty great.
-Yeah.

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:56.601
-That sums it all up.
It's perfect.

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:58.267
I want to show everyone a clip.
-Yes, please.

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:00.267
-Mike Myers in "Amsterdam."
Take a look.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.868
♪♪

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.701
-Paul Canterbury,
Canterbury Glass.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.000
London, England.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.133
We make the finest prosthetic
glass, industrial glass,

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.300
top-secret glass,
military glass,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.501
every kind of glass
except window glass.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:16.200
Unless, of course,
it's bulletproof.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.033
Have no fear, a friend of
Miss Valerie

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:19.701
is a friend of Paul Canterbury,

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:23.901
who offers you a lifetime supply
of Canterbury Glass eyes.

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:25.367
-Not too bad.
-As you can see,

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:27.634
I've got the same injury as you,
or perhaps you can't see,

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.968
due to the fine craftsmanship
of Canterbury Glass.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:34.734
-Who else can do that?
Who else can do that?

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.901
Mike Myers, everybody!

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:39.601
"Amsterdam" is in theaters now.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.467
Sutton Foster joins us
after the break.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.968
Stick around, everybody.

